Answer ((-(3 + -8 + -7 + -2) = -(10) ) - ( (-(2 + 8 + 1))) - -6 )) ; First, simplify the inner parentheses: Addition involving negative numbers results in a number smaller than one of the original numbers. For addition of negative numbers we just add the numbers as for positive ones and then put a minus sign in front of the result.( -(sum of (3 ,8 ,7 ,2)) = -10 )-( sum of( 2,8,1) is added to get 11)-(-6); Now adding within same operator: since there are equal number of negative numbers and positive number so the overall expression will be negative. Hence we need take minus (sum of absolute values of this terms). -( |-10| + | -11|) ; =-(|-10|+11) as above, Absolute value of a '-ve' no is '+ve' '10'. Now to get minuse in front of the result(or negative sign), we need one more minus from either of these absolute values i.e., -( |minused 10| +another positive number, say,'1') = - (|-(-10)|+1) ; [note: since module or abs value of a no is always non-negative. hence |-(-10)|=10] Now we have :-(10+1)=-11;
The answer is $\boxed{-11}$.

